# Cloud 3 packed Milky Way

Asset: `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/PaintedCloud/v04/Altitude/Cloud3_Wisp/T_Cloud3_MilkyWay_CloudMask_v02`.

RGB holds generated linear Milky Way radiance; A exactly preserves the previous Wisp EXR alpha. The 4096 x 2048 delivery is resampled from generated artwork, not native 4K or a measured HDR environment. Longitude and pole/horizon guards fade RGB to black. Alpha is unchanged.

Cloud 3 now reads A for coverage and shade. Its original independent R shading cannot be preserved in the same single alpha channel. RGB is sampled in world-direction lat-long, independently of cloud motion, and added to the night sky. Existing foreground cloud occlusion remains active. BP controls `MilkyWayIntensity` (0.65) and `MilkyWayRotation` (0 degrees) are under `Milky Way`.

Validation: BP and three materials compiled with no errors; dependency audit passed. Live MID readback confirmed new texture and intensity, with night gate 0 at noon and 1 at midnight. Original time was restored. No nighttime viewport visual comparison was performed.

Generated with the built-in imagegen tool. Prompt: Create a 2:1 equirectangular game sky texture on pure black, RGB additive Milky Way sky artwork. Elegant hand-painted realistic astronomical nebula, a sweeping soft diagonal galactic band with dusty dark fissures, pale pearl core, restrained lavender and cool blue with subtle warm dusty highlights, very fine scattered stars, no huge stars. Full width panorama. All visible galactic content lies in TOP HALF (upper celestial hemisphere); bottom half entirely pure black. Fade to pure black near left/right edges and near top edge and horizontal midline so seamless longitude wrapping and pole safe. No landscape, horizon objects, clouds, sun, moon, text, labels or watermark. Detailed but soft natural density, not a spiral galaxy viewed externally. Wide rectangular 2:1 canvas.
